  "tagline": "Continuous profiling database that stores CPU and memory profiles over time on object storage.",
  "description": "Grafana Pyroscope is a continuous-profiling backend: agents, eBPF collectors or SDKs send CPU, memory, lock and allocation profiles every few seconds, and Pyroscope stores them as time-indexed, deduplicated stack-trace data in object storage so you can compare flame graphs across releases, hosts or time ranges. Grafana Labs acquired the Pyroscope project in 2023 and merged it with its own Phlare database, so the current engine follows the Mimir/Loki architecture with distributors, ingesters and store-gateways. It is AGPL-3.0, integrates with Tempo to link spans to profiles, and is also offered as Grafana Cloud Profiles.",
